{"name":"Sun Deck","hex":"#f0dca0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sun deck","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of sundeck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sun_deck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Deck (ship)","blocks":[{"text":"A deck is a permanent covering over a compartment or a hull of a ship. On a boat or ship, the primary or upper deck is the horizontal structure that forms the \"roof\" of the hull, strengthening it and serving as the primary working surface. Vessels often have more than one level both within the hull and in the superstructure above the primary deck, similar to the floors of a multi-storey building, that are also referred to as decks, as are certain compartments and decks built over specific areas of the superstructure. Decks for some purposes have specific names."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Wrau-olympic-deck.jpg/330px-Wrau-olympic-deck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deck_(ship)","wikidata":"Q208123"},{"title":"Sun","blocks":[{"text":"The Sun is the star located at the centre of the Solar System. It is a massive sphere of hot plasma, heated to incandescence by nuclear fusion reactions in its core, radiating the energy from its surface mainly as visible light and infrared radiation, with 10% at ultraviolet energies. It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject of astronomical research since antiquity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun","wikidata":"Q525"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Falls_of_Clyde_deck.jpg/500px-Falls_of_Clyde_deck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Falls_of_Clyde_deck.jpg/500px-Falls_of_Clyde_deck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The upper deck of the Falls of Clyde is iron; a centre strip is planked with wood as a sort of walkway. As is typical for a late-19th-century vessel, several deckhouses may be seen.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFalls_of_Clyde_deck.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/22/QM2-wraparound-deck.jpg/500px-QM2-wraparound-deck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/22/QM2-wraparound-deck.jpg/500px-QM2-wraparound-deck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crew and passengers on the wraparound deck of RMS Queen Mary 2, an ocean liner","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQM2-wraparound-deck.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg/500px-Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg/1280px-Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg/500px-Vasa-weather_deck_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Weather deck of the Swedish 17th-century warship Vasa looking aft toward the sterncastle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVasa-weather_deck_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg/500px-Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg/1280px-Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg/500px-Pedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prince Regent Pedro of Braganza (pointing) and others on the deck of the Brazilian frigate União after the failed Avilez Rebellion, 1822","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APedro_I_of_Brazil_and_Avilez.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg/500px-Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg/1280px-Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg/500px-Sun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sun deck of MS Mariella","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_deck_of_Viking_Mariella.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/500px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/1280px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png/500px-Solar_System_True_Color_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut